# Engine-agnostic Spark configuration: which catalog exists, which jar
# implements it, what timezone. Rendered to spark-defaults.conf in the same
# directory by marketrank.config at import time -- see the note below.
#
# TWO consumers read the rendered file and they are disjoint:
#   * get_spark(), and anything that imports marketrank (pytest, notebooks,
#     a REPL), via SPARK_CONF_DIR which config.py sets with os.environ.setdefault
#   * dbt, which never imports marketrank, via the Makefile's export
#
# dbt-spark's "session" method builds its OWN SparkSession inside dbt's process,
# so the Iceberg jar coordinate and the catalog definition have to exist at
# session-construction time. This file is how both consumers get one definition.
#
# Runtime and topology configuration -- driver bind address, spill directory,
# driver memory, master -- deliberately does NOT live here. It is machine- and
# mode-dependent and stays in get_spark(), where it can branch.
#
# WHY THIS IS A TEMPLATE: the warehouse location is environment-dependent
# (MARKETRANK_WAREHOUSE; env.misha.sh sets a different one), and Spark does NOT
# interpolate environment variables in spark-defaults.conf -- a literal
# ${{env:MARKETRANK_WAREHOUSE}} is read as a relative path and the catalog fails
# with "Relative path in absolute URI". Verified, see BUILD_NOTES step 1.5.
# (Braces are doubled above because this file is rendered with str.format.)

spark.jars.packages                 org.apache.iceberg:iceberg-spark-runtime-3.5_2.12:{iceberg_version}
spark.sql.extensions                org.apache.iceberg.spark.extensions.IcebergSparkSessionExtensions
spark.sql.catalog.{catalog}         org.apache.iceberg.spark.SparkCatalog
spark.sql.catalog.{catalog}.type    hadoop
spark.sql.catalog.{catalog}.warehouse {warehouse}
spark.sql.defaultCatalog            {catalog}
spark.sql.session.timeZone          UTC

# Display only. The console progress bar interleaves carriage returns into any
# piped log and makes captured runs unreadable.
spark.ui.showConsoleProgress        false
